That's a great name. Yeah, I don't really want to drink anything from there.

00:27:30.580 --> 00:27:32.480
The Frothing Slosh.

00:27:32.880 --> 00:27:37.400
All right, so let's get into maybe some of the actual quests that you'll run into here.

00:27:37.580 --> 00:27:41.160
Because there are some interesting solutions.

00:27:41.660 --> 00:27:43.660
And interesting for the time, I should say.

00:27:43.800 --> 00:27:45.380
Like, obviously, we have better things now.

00:27:45.380 --> 00:27:55.260
But there are, you know, like, there's one where you have to, there's a spy and you have to catch the spy.

00:27:55.500 --> 00:28:00.420
So to catch the spy, again, because there's a day-night cycle, you have to wait by the gate at night.

00:28:00.580 --> 00:28:03.260
And then there's a guard who's sneaking out.

00:28:03.380 --> 00:28:04.280
You kill that guard.

00:28:04.280 --> 00:28:07.160
The spy looks just like every other guard.

00:28:07.600 --> 00:28:09.920
So there's no, like, real tell.

00:28:10.340 --> 00:28:18.000
So you just, so you might have to, like, kill a few to figure out, like, okay, at the end of the day, though.

00:28:18.160 --> 00:28:20.560
Very heroic shit. Right, I killed the spy.

00:28:21.040 --> 00:28:23.940
You know? So, sorry, a few people had to get in the way.

00:28:24.860 --> 00:28:27.160
You're going to have to break a little, break a few eggs.

00:28:28.460 --> 00:28:31.480
Yeah, I mean, there weren't rules on the quest.

00:28:31.640 --> 00:28:34.400
It was just, do, it was solve this problem.

00:28:34.640 --> 00:28:35.820
Yeah. Right. Solve it.

00:28:36.100 --> 00:28:48.160
One of the quests is sneaking up on a group of camping orcs, a family of orcs, and just, like, slaughtering them.

00:28:48.500 --> 00:28:50.720
Yeah, and not just the men, but the women and children, too.

00:28:50.720 --> 00:28:51.740
Yes, yes.

00:28:53.800 --> 00:29:02.260
That's a quest. There's one where you've got to sprinkle a little bit of holy water on, like, a zombie king.

00:29:04.560 --> 00:29:06.180
That's part, that's one of them.

00:29:08.240 --> 00:29:09.580
Yeah. That's it.

00:29:09.580 --> 00:29:16.360
It's, like, I feel like it's, yeah, there's, like, you've got to save the prince from the bandits for one of them.

00:29:16.440 --> 00:29:19.300
You've got to, like, find their hideout and kill them all again.

00:29:19.400 --> 00:29:20.620
Oh, is that the one you're talking about? Is that the same one?

00:29:21.900 --> 00:29:26.940
The goblin, not goblin, the orc one is the first, it's the first, like, actual quest.

00:29:27.400 --> 00:29:38.280
But what I, like, kind of thought was interesting, I feel like there's not a lot of games where there's, like, that we've played so far where there are these quests that are so different.

00:29:38.280 --> 00:29:44.640
They're almost, like, a pre-pre-pre-pre-precursor to, like, the Morrowind-type quest you're talking about.

00:29:45.080 --> 00:29:51.440
Where it's, like, oh, it's, like, it's just, like, there's actually just, like, stuff going on in this world and you have to go take care of it.

00:29:51.500 --> 00:29:57.020
And I know, like, Final Fantasy had stuff like that, too, but it was, like, it's, like, a little more designed where it's, like, yeah, go do this.

00:29:57.020 --> 00:29:59.780
And it's, like, what you have to go do is go fight these enemies.

00:30:00.620 --> 00:30:05.160
I think what's more interesting, right, is that, like, you can just go there and it'll be happening.

